# Google Earth Engine service-account credentials.
#
# The API routes (/api/ndvi, /api/lulc, /api/flood) authenticate with Earth
# Engine using a service account. Paste the ENTIRE service-account JSON key as a
# single-line value below (it is JSON.parse()'d at startup).
#
# How to obtain:
#   1. In Google Cloud, create a service account with the Earth Engine API enabled.
#   2. Register the service account at https://signup.earthengine.google.com/ (or
#      add it to an existing EE-enabled Cloud project).
#   3. Create a JSON key for the service account and paste its contents here.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the value. Never commit `.env.local`.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_KEY={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"...@....iam.gserviceaccount.com","client_id":"...","auth_uri":"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth","token_uri":"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token","auth_provider_x509_cert_url":"https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs","client_x509_cert_url":"..."}
